.layout = "docs.shtml",
---

sqlz has no separate binary. Every command runs through the build:

```console
$ zig build sqlz -- <command>
```

`--project NAME` selects a registered project and is inferred when only one
applies.

# [Implemented]($heading.id('implemented'))

## bootstrap postgres

Copies a SQLite database into a dedicated PostgreSQL schema: replays the
PostgreSQL head, transfers rows with bound parameters, restores sequences and
validates row counts.

```console
$ zig build sqlz -- bootstrap postgres --from-sqlite app.db \
    --postgres-url postgres://localhost/app [--wipe-postgres --yes]
```

| Flag | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `--from-sqlite PATH` | source SQLite database |
| `--postgres-url URL` | destination; falls back to `DATABASE_URL` |
| `--wipe-postgres` | reset an existing managed destination; requires `--yes` |
| `--project NAME` | registered project to use |

>[]($block.attrs('note'))
>The project needs both a SQLite and a PostgreSQL profile and a single-entry
>`search_path` other than `public`. This command is experimental.

# [Planned]($heading.id('planned'))

The full command surface for 0.1:

```
zig build sqlz -- init
zig build sqlz -- check [--project NAME] [--format human|json]
zig build sqlz -- status [--project NAME] --backend NAME
zig build sqlz -- migrate upgrade TARGET [connection options]
zig build sqlz -- migrate downgrade TARGET [connection options]
zig build sqlz -- revision create [--message TEXT]
zig build sqlz -- revision merge REV...
zig build sqlz -- state init|stamp|repair|rebind
zig build sqlz -- journal show|prune
```

Read-only commands never prompt. Destructive commands prompt on a terminal
and need `--yes` otherwise. `--format json` writes versioned JSON records to
stdout and everything else to stderr.
